      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-309596",
      ":question/problem": "A city council surveyed $250$ households to learn whether they were satisfied with the recycling services. Every household in the sample responded, and $82%$ indicated that they were satisfied. Based on this information, which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n1. Of all households in the city, $82%$ would say they are satisfied with the recycling services.\n2. If another random sample of $250$ households were surveyed, exactly $82%$ would say they are satisfied.\n3. The true proportion of satisfied households in the city is approximately $82%$."
    },
