      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-311007",
      ":question/problem": "A university surveyed $600$ students chosen at random and asked, \"Are you satisfied with the campus dining options?\" Of those surveyed, $71%$ responded that they were satisfied. Based on the results of the survey, which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n1. Of all students at the university, $71%$ are satisfied with the campus dining options.\n2. If another $600$ students were randomly surveyed at the university, exactly $71%$ of them would report satisfaction with the dining options.\n3. If $600$ students at a different university were surveyed, $71%$ would report satisfaction with their campus dining options."
    }
